// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-052
=adr: 052
=title: Passphrase-Derived Key Authentication (SuperAdmin) + Recovery (Admin)
=date: 2026-04-01
=status: accepted

#ctx
SuperAdmin (client) deploys Docker image to customer campus; system is air-gapped.
SuperAdmin needs to log in to any deployment without a stored password.
Admin must self-recover password without superadmin involvement.
No recovery codes; no email; no external authority after developer delivery.

#opts
opt1: Password-based superadmin + email recovery — fails in air-gapped environments
opt2: Static keypair file — can be lost; requires secure per-customer distribution
opt3: Passphrase-derived keypair baked in image — deterministic; re-derive from passphrase anytime

#decision
SuperAdmin authentication is KEY-BASED — no stored password in DB.
Derivation: PBKDF2(passphrase, salt='KOSMOS_RECOVERY_V1', iterations=600000, hash=SHA-256) → seed → RSA-2048.
Same passphrase always yields same keypair; no file to carry or back up.
Client generates public key from passphrase ONCE → bakes into Docker image: ARG SUPERADMIN_PUBLIC_KEY → ENV.
One keypair shared across ALL customer deployments; client maintains one passphrase only.
SuperAdmin login flow (browser-only, no CLI):
  1. GET /api/v1/auth/superadmin/challenge → HMAC challenge, valid 15 min
  2. Browser: enter passphrase → WebCrypto PBKDF2 derives private key → signs challenge
  3. POST /api/v1/auth/superadmin/login → server verifies signature vs. ENV public key → JWT session
Worst-case passphrase loss: rebuild image with new public key + redeploy to customer (acceptable).
Admin recovery (separate mechanism): Admin sets recovery passphrase at first login.
  Same derivation. Admin's public key stored in DB (recoveryPublicKey on User model).
  Recovery: GET /auth/recovery/challenge → browser signs → POST /auth/recovery/redeem → one-time reset.

#consequences
+ No password stored for superadmin; immune to DB credential leaks
+ One passphrase works for all deployments — client maintains one credential
+ Browser handles all crypto; no CLI required for login or recovery
+ Admin self-recovers independently; superadmin re-derives from passphrase at any time
- SuperAdmin passphrase loss = image rebuild + redeploy (client must store passphrase securely)
- Public key rotation = image rebuild (same as any baked secret; acceptable)
- WebCrypto requires secure context (HTTPS or localhost)

#scope
~new_backend: /auth/superadmin/challenge + /auth/superadmin/login (verify vs ENV public key)
~new_backend: /auth/recovery/challenge + /auth/recovery/redeem (verify vs DB recoveryPublicKey)
~new_frontend: SuperAdmin login page (passphrase field → WebCrypto derive+sign → session)
~new_frontend: Admin recovery passphrase setup (first-login modal) + recovery login flow (WebCrypto)
~docker: ARG SUPERADMIN_PUBLIC_KEY → ENV bake (same pattern as ADR-050 LICENSE_PUBLIC_KEY)
~user_model: recoveryPublicKey on User (admins only); superadmin record has no password field
~no_cli: platform-cli not required for auth or recovery; browser-only
